Reference diff: teach config.sub the *-forestos OS.

This documents the change build-toolchain.sh applies idempotently (via a
guarded sed insertion) to BOTH the binutils and gcc top-level config.sub.
The relevant anchor line differs slightly between binutils 2.43 and
gcc 13.2.0 (extra OS names after `fiwix*`), so the script keys off the
`fiwix*` token rather than applying this context diff verbatim.

--- a/config.sub
+++ b/config.sub
@@ (OS validation list, near the `fiwix*` entry)
 	     | nsk* | powerunix* | genode* | zvmoe* | qnx* | emx* | zephyr* \
-	     | fiwix* )
+	     | forestos* | fiwix* )
 		;;

For binutils 2.43 the same token line reads:
-	     | fiwix* | mlibc* | cos* | mbr* | ironclad* )
+	     | forestos* | fiwix* | mlibc* | cos* | mbr* | ironclad* )

Effect: `config.sub i686-forestos` and `config.sub x86_64-forestos`
canonicalize successfully instead of failing with
"Invalid configuration ... OS `forestos' not recognized".
